{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot","id":544413,"title":"Flavor Text Ideas for Donating Gnosis during Caern Moot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-07T16:16:30-07:00","id":544413,"title":"Flavor Text Ideas for Donating Gnosis during Caern Moot","content":"I'm looking at ideas for flavor text and examples of how Garou donate Gnosis, like to a Caern spirit during a moot.<br /> <br /> In the real world, temple sacrifices and such were done by sacrificing animals. Occasionally, this kind of blood sacrifice finds itself in Werewolf, usually by a Get of Fenris spilling his own blood to some spirit.<br /> <br /> Mechanically of course, the Gnosis just disappears from a character sheet. However, I'm interested in how people have done it or seen it happen in games. I assume most people have simply hand waved it (reduce your Gnosis by 1, and let's move on). However, I think at least some STs or players have done more. How do people see this happening? Just the Garou &quot;concentrating&quot; or &quot;meditating&quot; or &quot;praying&quot; and the Gnosis leaves them (essentially this means the Garou does nothing, at least physically)? Or does the Gnosis transfer because the Garou does <i>something</i> - make an animal sacrifice, burn incense, make some kind of formal proclamation, or perform an ecstatic dance that leaves physically and mentally exhausted?<br /> <br /> I'll be running a Caern Moot for the first time in game (as opposed to downtime), and I like to describe it in terms of real life - not game mechanics - as much as I can. While I think every Caern will be different based on its Totem, I think the vast majority of Caerns would likely have some kind of animal sacrifice. Of course, the game makes no mention of this. I'm wondering how people have seen it happen in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:51:28-07:00","id":544786,"title":"","content":"I don't have any in-game anecdotes for this, but I'm perusing Werewolf Player's Guide 2nd Ed (pp.93-96) to review the particular sections of a moot. Relevant excepts from this book are summed up below:<br /> <br /> The Opening Howl, led by the Master of the Howl (an office typically held by a Galliard), starts the moot. After the sept has finished howling, the Master of the Howl announces the purpose of the moot.<br /> <br /> The second part of the moot is The Inner Sky. The Caller of the Wyld leads the sept in this portion of the moot. Umbral spirits are the source of the caern's continued strength; as such, the Inner Sky is vital to the caern's health. The Caller of the Wyld must contact the spirits and treat them with appropriate honor and deference.<br /> <br /> The third part of the moot is called Cracking the Bone. This is when sept business is discussed, grievances are aired, and all temporal business is conducted at this time. Most tribes allow all Garou who wish to speak to do so. Even in this openness there is a proper procedure, however. The concept of rank is so ingrained in most Garou that lower ranking members inevitably defer to higher ranking individuals. A Garou who speaks out of turn, defying the sept hierarchy, invariably loses Honor. Still, some of the more tolerant septs, usually led by the Bone Gnawers or Children of Gaia, allow their younger members to speak out of turn without harsh penalty. The Garou system of justice is simpler than that used in the human world, as it has more in common with lupine ways. Judgment and the punishment that follows is swift, blunt and without appeal. Once a decision is made, for good or ill, the matter is usually closed.<br /> <br /> The fourth part of the moot is known as Stories and Songs and is led by the Talesinger. Tales of Garou heroism, old and new, are spun by the Talesinger. The nature of these stories depends on the tribe of the sept.<br /> <br /> Lastly is The Revel. This is the part of the moot where the Garou donate their Gnosis to the caern. Revels involve mock battles and other displays of strength and prowess erupt spontaneously throughout the sept, as the Garou prepare for the run. These demonstrations serve to take the Garou past the point of no return, a truly liberating release on every level. Once the sept reaches this degree of excitement, the Wyrm Foe thunders out of the caern proper, leading the entire sept on an exhausting run to clear the area around the caern of all enemies. During the run itself, many Garou eventually transform into their deadly Crinos form, as they fully embrace their Rage.<br /> <br /> Although any Garou in the throes of the Revel is a gloriously fearsome sight, the Get of Fenris are renowned for their incredible savagery during the run. The defense of caerns by the Get and other rural septs give rise to many small-town stories of &quot;full moon fever.&quot; Similarly, the urban prowls of Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker Revels are often labeled gang warfare or particularly vicious killing sprees by the unsuspecting human populace.<br /> <br /> The Garou passion released during the Revel is effectively raw Gnosis that pours back into the caern itself. Such recharging is vital in maintaining the caern's power, just as sustaining the caern's connection to the Umbra is. Every Garou who participates in a Revel must spend at least one point of Gnosis toward recharging the caern. An active caern must receive five points of Gnosis per<br /> power level each lunar month to remain fully replenished. Thus, to replenish a caern with a power level of four, the sept must spend at least 20 Gnosis. These points need not be spent all at once (although they usually are during a Revel), but can be given to the caern at any time during the month. A caern that doesn't receive the requisite amount of Gnosis lapses into inactive status. Although its potential spiritual energy still exists, the caern must be reconnected to the Umbra and its spirits awakened before Garou may tap its power.<br /> <br /> Black Fox, just out of curiosity, what tribe(s) are present at your caern?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T22:06:32-07:00","id":544795,"title":"","content":"I am running a historical chronicle in Germany. The tribes are near a major city. The sept includes mostly Silver Fangs and Get of Fenris, but Glass Walkers and sometimes Bone Gnawers can also be found there. Many of the surrounding septs are exclusively of one tribe, but this one is multi-tribal. However, my question is more general since the PCs may travel to other caerns at some point.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Revel is the relevant portion of the Moot when Gnosis is donated. The description as is seems to indicate it as a spontaneous outpouring of Gnosis from religious ecstasy, but it also implies Gnosis can be donated at other times - even not during the Moot, and this is where I think it's possible for Gnosis to be donated in other ways such as religious animal sacrifice or other means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:23:23-07:00","id":547976,"title":"","content":"As varied as the spirits that inhabit the world.<br /> <br /> In our games, we've run the donation in all kinds of ways, including some unscrupulous and cunning sorts finding ways to trick others into sacrificing more than they might otherwise intend. Some thoughts from ways I've run it or seen it run:<br /> <br /> The type of Caern it is, and the Caern's Totem(s) and local Spirits should definitely be kept in mind when a Garou is wanting to donate Gnosis. You wouldn't necessary peacefully meditate in the glen of a Caern of Rage to return your own essence to the land - in some situations providing in inappropriate sacrifice or method could even be disrespectful. Sacrifice in the form of harm or slaying would be anathema to Caerns of peace, tranquility, or the like, and would at the very least simply not count toward the Gnosis. Theoretically Caerns that receive a great deal donations in in forms that are antithetical to the Caern's purpose and spirit would poison it, if somehow left uncorrected - although it would have to be <i>a</i> <i><u>really</u> terrible</i> Sept and Keeper of the Land to let things get so far.<br /> <br /> Shrines of Adoration were often used in our games, and gifts imparted to those sites also trickled to the Caern, so any positive spiritual behaviour appropriate for the Caern would maintain the spiritual ecology of the place. When Moot time came, the donation of Gnosis during the revel, the expenditure was done over the course of the sweat and body heat of exertion, the depth of feeling in the sense of community, the closeness reinforced to their purpose, exuded in their very breath. I often imagined it like a mist or fog - not physically, but metaphorically - all of that vital life from the Sept affirming its bonds to each other, to the land, to Gaia, creating this spiritual miasma where nothing was left untouched, all breath was shared, and in that way, so too was that energy exchanged.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, there was often plenty of blood-letting. Blood was usually the ol' stand by. In arid regions especially, blood and saliva often made up the token gesture of the donations, returning some moisture to the land, if they had nothing else appropriate to offer as a physical, tangible thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:25:05-07:00","id":549751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot?p=547976#post547976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In arid regions especially, blood and saliva often made up the token gesture of the donations, returning some moisture to the land, if they had nothing else appropriate to offer as a physical, tangible thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this a lot. It reminds me of Dune when the Fremen spit at Duke Atreides to show respect because bodily fluids were so precious to them. I'll remember that if my game ever has a scene at a desert caern.<br /> <br /> If people are looking for specifics, is the Caern Totem good to know? Here are several kinds in the region:<br /> <br /> Catfish<br /> Fog<br /> Woodpecker<br /> Boar<br /> Swan<br /> Goose<br /> Honeybee<br /> Mountain<br /> Lion<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T04:55:36-07:00","id":549969,"title":"","content":"&quot;He shall know your ways as if born to them.&quot; ;D<br /> <br /> I'll post up some thoughts for each of those Totems after work tomorrow. Do you have the Caern Type for each of those, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":2810,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","user":"Yakecen-Sings","date":". 06-11-2015, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:02:10-07:00","id":550670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot?p=549751#post549751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this a lot. It reminds me of Dune when the Fremen spit at Duke Atreides to show respect because bodily fluids were so precious to them. I'll remember that if my game ever has a scene at a desert caern.<br /> <br /> If people are looking for specifics, is the Caern Totem good to know? Here are several kinds in the region:<br /> <br /> Catfish<br /> Fog<br /> Woodpecker<br /> Boar<br /> Swan<br /> Goose<br /> Honeybee<br /> Mountain<br /> Lion</div> </div> </div> </div>Are those supposed to be the types of spirits in the region or totems that are in neighboring caerns in the area? because aside from Goose, Fog, Boar and Lion, those aren't canon totem spirits that I recognize. They're certainly not in my Totem List, so if these are published totems, I'd like page references for them except for Goose, Fog, Boar and Lion (which, incidentally, are in my list already). As for the types of totems that Goose, Fog, Boar and Lion are, here's the rundown:<br /> <br /> Goose: unknown (Wendigo Revised forgot to say which type of totems the Wendigo totems are) but I'm guesing Wisdom from its write-up<br /> <br /> Fog: Wisdom<br /> <br /> Boar: War<br /> <br /> Lion: Respect (Keep in mind, Lion has 2 different write-ups depending on whether the White Howlers have fallen or not, as well as a 3rd write-up from W20 Rage Across the World that is the most recent write-up, i.e. published with updated W20 rules.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Is Woodpecker supposed to be Red-cockaded Woodpecker? Because that totem is also in my list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 06-11-2015, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:32:11-07:00","id":550715,"title":"","content":"The type of Caern isn't always an exact match to the &quot;Renown Type&quot; of the Totem Spirit. I'm after the type of the Caern, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T17:47:15-07:00","id":550925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot?p=550715#post550715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The type of Caern isn't always an exact match to the &quot;Renown Type&quot; of the Totem Spirit. I'm after the type of the Caern, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>True dat. I'm just hoping Black Fox will clarify what he was talking about when he made that list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T00:27:44-07:00","id":551158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot?p=549969#post549969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll post up some thoughts for each of those Totems after work tomorrow. Do you have the Caern Type for each of those, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>It always gets more complicated than I intended. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Catfish - Caern of Harmony (Wisdom); takes place in a city with lots of rivers/lakes that bring unity to its various parts<br /> Fog - Caern of Mystery (Wisdom); takes place on a mountaintop known for spooky legends<br /> Woodpecker - Caern of Strength (Glory); representing the persistence of the woodpecker making holes in the tree all day; in one of the great primeval forests<br /> Boar - Caern of Courage (Glory); happens at an old battlefield reknown for its slaughter<br /> Swan - Caern of Dignity (Honor); representing dignity of patrician families in a city; a Glass Walker urban sept<br /> Goose - Caern of Streetwise (Wisdom); representing street smarts on the docks of a port city; a Bonegnawer urban sept<br /> Honeybee - Caern of Kingship (Honor); very ancient (pre-medieval) familial seat of former royal family, now nobles of the land<br /> Mountain - Caern of Healing (Wisdom); represents the mountain spirit Rubezahl in the Krkonose mountains which is the source of the River Elbe. Rubezahl is the lord of the mountain and master of storms and rains that fall there<br /> Lion - Caern of Ancestors (wisdom); caern is ancestral home of ancient Norman nobles who were in service to William the Conqueror<br /> <br /> The Totem aren't always &quot;natural&quot; for their type, but made sense. For example, Lion is in the Normandy caern because lion is on the court of arms of Normandy and natural as the home for someone who would found a royal dynasty, but the caern itself represents heritage and therefore ancestors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot?p=550670#post550670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Woodpecker supposed to be Red-cockaded Woodpecker? Because that totem is also in my list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in particular. Woodpecker would be in Europe, so it would not be this particular breed which I believe is limited to southeastern North America.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T04:20:48-07:00","id":551239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/544413-flavor-text-ideas-for-donating-gnosis-during-caern-moot?p=551158#post551158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always gets more complicated than I intended. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Any opportunity to dig ever deeper into the spirituality and culture is one I relentless pursue with any who will feed me with conversation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A few quick blabs before I turn in for the night, brain is beat from work.<br /> <br /> Catfish - Caern of Harmony (Wisdom);<br /> <br /> Donations done in groups, especially as acts (whatever those may be) between packs that integrate each pack into the Sept whole. Physical exertion in the form of challenges/exercise/play that require teamwork - or simply cannot be completed without the tandem effort of many. Ritualistic bathing or swimming in the Protectorate's waters. If the Rite of Going To Water is known, it could be part of a personal cleansing and 'centering' done to restore harmony to the self, and thus to the whole (also, Baptism themes). I'm not familiar with Catfish's specific bans and demands, though, so I'm drawing a blank on token objects or tangible donations that the Gnosis might be imparted as.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fog - Caern of Mystery (Wisdom);<br /> <br /> Breath vapor, steam, incense (or whatever is regionally appropriate) smoke. Burning of written secrets, dedicated to Fog and none other. Donations performed in seclusion and secrecy, or only certain people (pack, the Master of the Rite or the Keeper of the Land). For Lupus especially, the covering of scent and games of stalking and stealth throughout the less rigid parts of the Moot, evasion replacing the more combative parts of the Revel. The scouring, purging of threats aspects of the Revel more focused on observation and learning to root out the knowledge of where the threats have arisen from, before they are purged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:51:19-07:00","id":552541,"title":"","content":"Yakecen, this is great stuff. I hope you continue your posts on this thread. It's really getting the hamster in my head to start running on the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:01:38-07:00","id":552880,"title":"","content":"Boar - Caern of Courage (Glory);<br /> <br /> Break out the war trophies. Challenges of endurance, exhilaration, and balls-to-the-wall feats of daring. Trophies of particular, local, or personal importance involved in whatever symbolic offering is made; drank from, used to serve or hold, used as part of the Moot rhythms like clacking tusks and cracking skulls. Trophies might be destroyed or otherwise ownership thereof relinquished in the process, so that one does not grow content and complacent, and is thusly always driven to seek out new foes and challenges. Not only for personal glory, but the cultivation of heroic deeds to come, in the form of &quot;meditation&quot; (term used very loosely) for rooting out fears and facing them directly, boldly, and offering up that overcoming of fear as a sacrifice; to replace one's future cowardice with future courage. Or, more crassly, Fear Factor-style games and tests of the self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T10:29:04-07:00","id":553190,"title":"","content":"I think Yakecen is conflating Caern Totems with Caern Types. The two are not the same and I'm not sure they're related in any way, at least rules-wise, although some totems are thematically more appropriate for particular caern types (I doubt you'd see Boar as the caern totem for a caern of Calm, for example). It looks to me like Yakecen is inventing new totems to go with his new caern types, which I heartily approve of. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> As for the Catfish Totem, Yakecen, it's an unofficial/unpublished totem so if you're &quot;unfamiliar&quot; with its traits and bans, it's because they don't exist yet. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> My suggestion? Just make something up that seems appropriate. It's not like there are any hard-and-fast rules for creating totems (although I would prefer to have some published guidelines). <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Same thing for your other totems with the exceptions of Lion, Boar, Fog and Goose (those four are previously published and in my Totems List).<br /> <br /> But in any case, these are very intriguing caern types. And the rules do allow for the rarity and even uniqueness of some caern types. (Caern of Humility, anyone?) Like Bent-Bow, an Uktena Theurge, said: &quot;If you've seen one caern, you've seen one caern.&quot; (Guardians of the Caerns, p.18)<br /> <br /> Now that I've glanced through the 2003 Players guide to Garou, I'm wondering if Yakecen and I are conflating/confusing Harmony caerns with Unity caerns? I haven't seen any references to &quot;Harmony&quot; caerns in the books (not yet anyway, but I'm still looking) but Unity caerns are definitely mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:22:57-07:00","id":553508,"title":"","content":"I find the list of Caern types in the core books and the few supplements I have limiting, so I very often make up my own. <br /> <br /> I come up with a theme for the caern, and then decide on the kind of spirit that fits two things - 1 what kind of spirit fits the caern type and 2) what kind of spirit makes sense for the region. My preference is for the spirit to actually reflect the area - what kind of wildlife does it have, what kind of geography, what is the area well known for. Sometimes I go for the thematic more than actual (there are no lions where the Lion totem is, but Lions are part of the Coat of Arms of the local area and families in it).<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible for the same spirit to be a Totem of very different caern types provided the spirit still seems appropriate for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T16:31:54-07:00","id":553532,"title":"","content":"I'm looking at a blending of both; what the Type of Caern is, mixed with who and what the resident Totem of the Caern is. Sometimes they line up very well, being almost indistinguishable, and sometimes they are very different and have appropriately more complex responsibilities. Just rough ideas, like different colors to inspire Black Fox, regardless of if he uses any of the hues I toss out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have to bolt for a D&amp;D game, but I'll be back to idea-spit about the remaining Caerns and Totems later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:27:25-07:00","id":657638,"title":"","content":"This is a little old, but I hope it's ok to still add to this.<br /> <br /> In games I've played or STd I've seen and created a few ways to donate gnosis during a moot or even as an offering/sacrifice to the spirits of a caern.<br /> <br /> perhaps these will help too.<br /> <br /> For Galliards when telling a tale, song or dance to spend a point of gnosis at the end and let it pour out of mouth as vapoured breath.<br /> <br /> As Theurges, take part in a traditional offering/ritual of the Indiginous peoples and spend a point. (The ritual or tradition being somethinh the local spirits would know of or seen for generations)<br /> <br /> Or if they have the Knowledge Dpirit Lore (or even cosmology if I'm generous) to forge their gnosis into an item the spitit would appreciate. An arrow for war, corn/maize, a goblet, a knife, etc etc. Something that would resonate or be appreciated before being absorbed.<br /> <br /> a lupus creating gnosis fleas or bugs within its fur for a bird spirit to pluck out is another.<br /> <br /> For Ahrouns, battle, challenges, or recognition of their bravery and valor. Swearing dutiful dedication and zeal to the protection and defense of the land and giving their blood to the land and letting it flow through them.<br /> <br /> For philodoxes reminding of the laws, sworn duty to gaia and place of purpose and reciting the bans and laws of the spirit that patrons the caern. an honorable declaration and oath then spending a gnosis.<br /> <br /> For Ragabash, anyway they please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> they are the new moon after all.<br /> <br /> it can get even more diverse and interesting by offering something of Tribe as well as auspice in my experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:41:45-07:00","id":658860,"title":"","content":"These are good contributions, thank.<br /> <br /> At least it shows there are other people like me who do like thinking about the actual acts/events first and game mechanics second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T00:25:17-07:00","id":659033,"title":"","content":"You are very welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes I do like thinking and portraying ideas and themes, rituals and traditions into games and encouraging the players to develop it icly and run with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}